{
  "about": "A preview frame (core §2.4.2, CORE-K5; CUX §2.3, CUX-E1): an anet.message/1 whose body is a ChatMsg of kind stream_preview with every key a frame may carry (1, 2, 4-7, 9, 11-13). A one-shot envelope: outer key 8 = inner exp = inner ts + 60000. Sealed in two layers, the second to the recipient's (the requester's) interaction key in the interaction; the inner carries rk (15) and none of keys 10, 11, 12, 14, and is signed by the sender's key at key_state_seq 1 over the preimage v2 with 33 = ikid and 34 = enc2. Written by gen_v016.py with the ephemeral keys DeriveKeyPair(seed(\"ikmE\")) and DeriveKeyPair(seed(\"ikmE2\")); the Go test opens it, reproduces the preimage, the signature check, env_digest and ack_key, decodes the body as a ChatMsg and checks it with ValidatePreview. A one-shot envelope yields no token, so there is no handle or tok. negatives: envelopes refused by the seal layer, with their reason; body_negatives: frame bodies refused when they decode (decode) or by ValidatePreview (validate).",
